<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Enkomi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Enkomi is an archaeological site near Famagusta on the east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, one of the chief towns of the island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>. It had a harbour, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> workshops and ashlar buildings, and its finds include the bronze statue known as the Horned God and Cypro-Minoan tablets. It was abandoned in the 11th century BCE as its people moved to nearby Salamis.</p></div>
